        <briefdescription>
<para>Parse a search-result page into a structured <ref refid="structthemis_1_1scraper_1_1_search_result_page" kindref="compound">SearchResultPage</ref>. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Heuristic detection order:<orderedlist>
<listitem><para>JSON-LD / microdata structured data</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Common CSS patterns: ol.results li, ul.results li, div.result, article.result, .search-result, [data-result]</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Generic list fallback: largest <itemizedlist>
<listitem>
</listitem>
</itemizedlist>
<orderedlist>
<listitem>
</listitem>
</orderedlist>
item count</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para>For openjur.de the relevant container is <computeroutput>.result-list &gt; li</computeroutput>.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>html</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Raw HTML of the result page. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>base_url</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Absolute URL (for resolving relative links). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>selector</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Optional CSS-like selector hint (class or id prefix such as &quot;.result-list&quot; or &quot;#results&quot;); empty = auto. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Parsed <ref refid="structthemis_1_1scraper_1_1_search_result_page" kindref="compound">SearchResultPage</ref>. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
